WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.092
A useful analytical report combines a clear question, numerical summaries, an appropriate visual,

00:00:07.092 --> 00:00:14.217
and a short interpretation. The example asks how order amount differs across regions.

00:00:14.217 --> 00:00:21.637
We calculate count, mean, and median, then create a boxplot to compare the group distributions.

00:00:22.201 --> 00:00:24.398
Read the table and chart together.

00:00:24.398 --> 00:00:27.143
The table provides exact values.

00:00:27.143 --> 00:00:31.318
The boxplot helps you see differences in center and spread.

00:00:31.318 --> 00:00:36.488
If the table and chart seem to tell different stories, investigate why.

00:00:36.488 --> 00:00:43.653
For example, an extreme value may increase the mean while the median stays relatively stable.

00:00:43.653 --> 00:00:47.113
A good report does not end with code output.

00:00:47.113 --> 00:00:54.106
End with a sentence that explains what the evidence suggests and any limitations that affect the interpretation.
